strings |id, value|

bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    textarea_4x_device_height_not_in_ancestor_2026-11-27, 0, "At device scale 4 Chrome 159 lays a rows=10 textarea (13.333px monospace, padding 0, border 0) out 630 device px tall (157.5 CSS, 1x: 150) with a 63 px line pitch, and an auto-height overflow:hidden wrapper (padding-bottom:1px) grows with it to 634. Simple keeps the CSS box at 150, paints the textarea taller through its device-extra-height, but the wrapper stays at 4 x 151 = 604 and its clip cuts the textarea there; Simple's value line pitch is 60 device px."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    textarea_4x_device_height_not_in_ancestor_2026-11-27, P3, open, "4x textarea device height delta is not carried by its auto-height ancestor (wrapper 604 vs Chrome 634; line pitch 60 vs 63)", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_engine.spl, 2006, "AUTO_WRAP_PAGE in test/01_unit/browser_engine/textarea_value_clip_chrome159_spec.spl at k=4: Chrome yellow strip rows 630-633, Simple none (textarea white to 603, body from 604)", 2026-11-27, 2026-11-27, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    textarea_4x_device_height_not_in_ancestor_2026-11-27, 0, "2026-11-27 webrender-textarea-clip Linux aarch64 seed cargo-target-wr-seed1126b (sha256 fb80903917d6d5f5), Chrome for Testing 159.0.8154.6 --force-device-scale-factor=4 --hide-scrollbars, 400x300: Chrome textarea rows 0-629, wrapper strip 630-633, next block 634. Simple: textarea background to 603, next block 604. The block path records box_device_extra_h only from the cursor fraction (layout_engine.spl ~5558), so a child form control's device extra never reaches the parent. Paint clamps the textarea's grown clip edge to the wrapper's applied edge (_html_draw_ir_far_edge_delta), so nothing paints past 604."

bug_fix_strategies |bug_id, line_num, content|
    textarea_4x_device_height_not_in_ancestor_2026-11-27, 0, "Either carry the child control's device extra into the parent's device bottom (and the clip edge it owns), or size the textarea in device-scaled line metrics so its CSS height is 157.5 at k=4 like Chrome. Pin with the AUTO_WRAP_PAGE strip rows 630-633 and the 63 px pitch."
